    {
      "id": "h70837rvq",
      "node_id": "node-skinsense-07496689",
      "version_tag": "v1",
      "title": "Skinsense",
      "description": {
        "text": {
          "text": {
            "text": {
              "text": {
                "text": {
                  "text": {
                    "text": "Classifies skin lesions using an ensemble of three CNN models with patient metadata integration.\n\nThis node performs multi‑modal skin lesion classification using an ensemble of EfficientNetV2‑M, ConvNeXtV2‑Tiny, and Swin Transformer models, augmented with patient metadata (age, sex, anatomical site). It loads a pre‑trained ensemble package that contains the three image backbones and a meta‑model (e.g., logistic regression) that fuses their probability outputs with encoded metadata. The input image is resized to 560×560, normalized with ImageNet statistics, and transformed to a tensor. Age is scaled with a pre‑trained scaler; sex and site are one‑hot encoded using label encoders. Each backbone processes the image and concatenates its feature vector with processed metadata to produce class probabilities. The meta‑model then combines the three probability vectors and the raw metadata to output final probabilities across five lesion types (bcc, bkl, mel, nv, sq_spectrum). The node caches the predictor on first invocation to avoid reloading for subsequent calls. It returns a human‑readable string containing the full lesion name, short code, confidence percentage, and a risk level (low/high), enabling rapid clinical triage and decision support.",
                    "lineHeight": 14,
                    "fontSize": 11,
                    "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
                  },
                  "lineHeight": 14,
                  "fontSize": 11,
                  "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
                },
                "lineHeight": 14,
                "fontSize": 11,
                "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
              },
              "lineHeight": 14,
              "fontSize": 11,
              "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
            },
            "lineHeight": 14,
            "fontSize": 11,
            "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
          },
          "lineHeight": 14,
          "fontSize": 11,
          "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
        },
        "lineHeight": 14,
        "fontSize": 11,
        "fontFamily": "-apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "node_id": "node-skinsense-07496689",
        "name": "Skinsense",
        "description": "Classifies skin lesions using an ensemble of three CNN models with patient metadata integration.\n\nThis node performs multi‑modal skin lesion classification using an ensemble of EfficientNetV2‑M, ConvNeXtV2‑Tiny, and Swin Transformer models, augmented with patient metadata (age, sex, anatomical site). It loads a pre‑trained ensemble package that contains the three image backbones and a meta‑model (e.g., logistic regression) that fuses their probability outputs with encoded metadata. The input image is resized to 560×560, normalized with ImageNet statistics, and transformed to a tensor. Age is scaled with a pre‑trained scaler; sex and site are one‑hot encoded using label encoders. Each backbone processes the image and concatenates its feature vector with processed metadata to produce class probabilities. The meta‑model then combines the three probability vectors and the raw metadata to output final probabilities across five lesion types (bcc, bkl, mel, nv, sq_spectrum). The node caches the predictor on first invocation to avoid reloading for subsequent calls. It returns a human‑readable string containing the full lesion name, short code, confidence percentage, and a risk level (low/high), enabling rapid clinical triage and decision support.",
        "category": "llm",
